Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Compiling to Cyclic Tag Systems", "Title",
 CellID->851507790, ExpressionUUID->"976d63af-d107-0047-9a4b-f8ce4759c8c1"],

Cell["\<\
This tech note explains how CyclicTagCompiler turns cellular automata and \
automata networks into cyclic tag systems, one simple stage at a time, and \
how to decode the evolution of a cyclic tag system back to the evolution of \
the system it emulates.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->906048359, ExpressionUUID->"12a878df-c466-a048-87f4-539bf60422de"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Introduction", "Section",
 CellID->765158308, ExpressionUUID->"899d6caa-abe8-0b44-ad6d-d4f9f93a8098"],

Cell["\<\
A cyclic tag system is a very simple system that can nevertheless do any \
computation. This has made cyclic tag systems a useful step in showing that \
other simple systems are universal, such as the rule 110 cellular automaton \
and Wolfram's 2,3 Turing machine.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->944594762, ExpressionUUID->"b9303a38-bd01-b941-bb2c-198da3c1b6cf"],

Cell["\<\
There are three known routes for compiling Turing machines to cyclic tag \
systems. One goes from a Turing machine to a 2-symbol Turing machine, then to \
a tag system and then to a cyclic tag system. Another goes from a 2-symbol \
Turing machine to a Minsky register machine, then to a Fractran program and \
then to a cyclic tag system. Both are fairly simple, but both encode the \
state in unary, so the cyclic tag system is exponentially slower than the \
machine it emulates. The third route goes through clockwise Turing machines \
and avoids the exponential slowdown, but it is much more complicated.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->465152263, ExpressionUUID->"1cc5ccc0-d57c-2645-95df-876473e388e4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "CyclicTagCompiler implements a newer route that is both simple and free of \
the exponential slowdown: a cellular automaton or an automata network is \
compiled to an oblivious ring machine, that to an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula", ExpressionUUID->
  "ce22ea3d-bc81-384e-a5eb-5eb27f444b53"],
 "-ary cyclic tag system, and that to a cyclic tag system. Each stage is \
short and easy to follow, and none encodes numbers in unary."
}], "Text",
 CellID->392889331, ExpressionUUID->"bb4e9f10-59b9-7f4f-b1c4-23de7164efd3"],

Cell["\<\
The price is that the systems are finite: a cellular automaton is emulated on \
a cyclic tape of a fixed number of cells. Real computers are finite too, and \
some universality proofs, such as the one for Wolfram's 2,3 Turing machine, \
only need many finite cyclic tag systems, each run for a finite number of \
steps. The other known routes to cyclic tag systems may be added to \
CyclicTagCompiler later.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->18461942, ExpressionUUID->"067c8851-c544-3b4f-bdbd-f1d72570114d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The method, including compiling sequential automata networks to oblivious \
ring machines to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "f749114b-c9f1-db4a-8944-2bb2ed4a98bb"],
 "-ary cyclic tag to cyclic tag was worked out by Seth Marshall. Eric James \
Parfitt found the simpler compilation of cellular automata and the \
compilation of more parallel automata networks, and wrote this implementation."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0007703445114136`*^9},
 CellID->775356942,ExpressionUUID->"57a44155-87d4-0c41-8909-af3dc762d78e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Load the paclet:", "Text",
 CellID->679917114, ExpressionUUID->"543351e4-a286-d342-a56c-bad1fb51cd3a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<EricJamesParfitt`CyclicTagCompiler`\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",
 CellID->777064241, ExpressionUUID->"be53537d-5f5c-f347-a983-3c65d814077b"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Cyclic Tag Systems", "Section",
 CellID->814110646, ExpressionUUID->"7f1eae90-201c-f243-b261-94e07254ff00"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A cyclic tag system has a tape of 0s and 1s and a list of appendants that \
it uses in turn. At each step it deletes the first cell of the tape, and if \
that cell was 1, it appends the current appendant to the end of the tape. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["CyclicTagSystem",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->
    "paclet:EricJamesParfitt/CyclicTagCompiler/ref/CyclicTagSystem"]], 
  "InlineFormula", ExpressionUUID->"f7f7221c-c56e-2c4f-903b-37b35584d986"],
 " runs cyclic tag systems:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->157153821, ExpressionUUID->"a9b7fe85-2d6e-4941-bc6c-90d4accd41ff"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Run a cyclic tag system with appendants ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}]], "InlineFormula", ExpressionUUID->
  "19cd893c-2e12-3e4e-950f-8fd3895d8e4a"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"{", "0", "}"}]], "InlineFormula", ExpressionUUID->
  "c61c4e6e-c77e-934e-80b3-63c0ee4b9250"],
 " for 6 steps:"
}], "MathCaption",
 CellID->428324517, ExpressionUUID->"f750f873-2536-f145-81c3-ed5c97085b06"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"CyclicTagSystem", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "0", "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", "1", "}"}], ",", " ", "6"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",
 CellID->323922974, ExpressionUUID->"a7bc772b-9cb6-eb42-ab63-e3367198cf19"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "1", "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "1"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", "1", ",", "1"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "1"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "1", ",", "1"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "1", ",", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[1]=",
 CellID->808745307, ExpressionUUID->"8c02bab1-e11a-fd49-ba09-559cd52ef494"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["n-ary Cyclic Tag Systems", "Section",
 CellID->25226445, ExpressionUUID->"46fb9721-7a73-0c41-a954-810eddec3de2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "An ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula", ExpressionUUID->
  "d0498021-4f85-ae44-9d35-e91510225265"],
 "-ary cyclic tag system has a tape of symbols from 0 to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula", ExpressionUUID->
  "fb366a22-3529-3c40-922b-97da34345433"],
 "-1. Each part of its rule gives an appendant for each symbol, and at each \
step the system deletes the first symbol and appends the appendant for that \
symbol from the current rule part. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["NaryCyclicTag",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->
    "paclet:EricJamesParfitt/CyclicTagCompiler/ref/NaryCyclicTag"]], 
  "InlineFormula", ExpressionUUID->"d027ee34-64f4-c64e-9bf3-c0c23e6d9358"],
 " runs ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula", ExpressionUUID->
  "c0fccc04-f60f-ca44-819d-0c0df1bc76b0"],
 "-ary cyclic tag systems:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->567517556, ExpressionUUID->"4a253a52-2c60-984d-9610-6d7220743969"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["A 3-symbol system with two rule parts:", "MathCaption",
 CellID->246248158, ExpressionUUID->"73345535-31c9-fb40-b4a8-5c57f7fb6a0a"],

